{
  "summary": "P1 lost laptop (KB-021). Reporter: Mei Chen (user_id 9, Operations, Logistics Analyst, not VIP). She believes she left work laptop BL-LT-0109 (macOS 15) in an Uber last night and doesn't know if it was locked. Device status: shows ONLINE, last check-in 2026-10-11 02:35 UTC (Sat Oct 10, 21:35 Chicago). No warnings, 14.6% disk free. Sign-in logs (14 days): all 10 sign-ins are successful from Chicago with Duo push, residential/corporate networks, during usual hours. Latest was Fri Oct 9 08:23. Nothing suspicious since then, no failures. Account is active with VPN access. Data at risk: Operations/logistics data, a nearly full M365 mailbox (99.4%), and saved VPN/M365 sessions. Action taken: block_sign_in requested and waiting for tech approval. Still needed: remote lock/wipe of BL-LT-0109 while it's online, password reset after identity is confirmed by phone (number on file), session revocation, and a replacement device. Waiting on the user for when/where it was last seen and whether she has contacted Uber.",
  "reason": "KB-021 says always escalate lost devices for remote lock/wipe. Ticket is P1."
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Mei, thanks for reporting this so quickly. Here's what we're doing to protect your account and the laptop: 1) We've asked a technician to block sign-ins to your work account for now, so nobody can use a saved session on the laptop. Once it's approved, you won't be able to sign in or use VPN until we reset your password. We'll call you on the number we have on file to confirm it's you and give you the new password. 2) Our Tier 2 team has the ticket so they can remotely lock the laptop, or wipe it if needed. Please reply with: about what time and where you last had the laptop, which Uber trip it was (the date and rough route help), and whether you've reported it to Uber yet. If you haven't, please report the lost item in the Uber app now. If you think it was stolen and not just left behind, please also file a police report. Don't sign in to your work account from other devices until we call you.",
  "internal_note": "P1 lost device per KB-021. User Mei Chen (id 9) has laptop BL-LT-0109 (macOS 15). It shows ONLINE, last check-in 2026-10-11 02:35 UTC (Oct 10, 21:35 CT). Sign-in logs for the last 14 days look clean: all from Chicago with Duo push, during usual hours, latest Oct 9. User doesn't know if the laptop was locked, so I queued block_sign_in (approval id 1, pending). Escalated to Tier 2 (escalation id 1) for remote lock/wipe while the device is online, session revocation, and a replacement laptop. Next steps: confirm identity by phone using the number on file, then reset the password and give it to her by phone. Mailbox is at 99.4% of quota, which is a separate issue. Asked the user for when/where it was last seen and whether she has reported it to Uber.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-021"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
